On 7 May 2010 15:17, Luke Bergen <lukeabergen@gmail.com> wrote:

> Both seem like pretty useful constructs.  Whichever one is "correct", how
> would one express the other meaning?


For "fifty or sixty people" (meaning "between fifty and sixty people"), I
would like to use "bi'i", but I'm not sure whether {muno bi'i xano prenu}
would be valid. {li muno bi'i xano} seems valid as a mex though.

